  "id": "Compound::DB00716 - Gene::10800",
  "verbalization": "Nedocromil is likely to interact with Cysltr1 through a shared pathway involving Cysltr2. The evidence suggests that Nedocromil binds to Cysltr2, which then participates in leukotriene receptor activity, a process that is also associated with Cysltr1. This implies a potential functional link between Nedocromil and Cysltr1, possibly through the modulation of leukotriene signaling. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Nedocromil influences Cysltr1, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a role for Cysltr2 as a bridge between Nedocromil and Cysltr1, underscoring the importance of receptor participation in mediating drug effects.",
